atio is shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "We see that the point $(3,4)$ lies on the graph. Let's write the ratio $3:4$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can not simplify this fraction further. Hence, we can say that the graph shows the ratio $3:4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "309e24a1-6c8c-5705-beca-001fed696acc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Ratio From a Graph: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382e2ac0-f3a8-5ac4-8c61-9c2bc47cefdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454995} {:answer/id #uuid "c8532e8f-1e11-5ab5-a826-29c0b2a1b0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455247} {:answer/id #uuid "c90aabe3-00da-5a03-ab00-efa95a2ab8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455249} {:answer/id #uuid "d38dddcb-1ba4-546c-9c3c-ddceea90631d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455272} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b631b9-b038-5761-ba16-e29cc561bd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c90aabe3-00da-5a03-ab00-efa95a2ab8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455249} :answer-field/id #uuid "911476e4-bbe7-5564-815b-0e4c85c707f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5486d651-e419-5bc9-92fb-f6314f16f8ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-93311" :question/problem "![](images/89/895e7c02241a561dad88f45f67d1b52de966925bcc8ee5c7a3a840b209a1ef7c.png)\n\nDorothy is mixing red and yellow paints to make a particular shade of orange. The amount of red paint she needs for a given amount of yellow paint is shown above. In its simplest form, what is the ratio of red to yellow paint in this mix?" :question/worked-solution "One of the points belonging to the graph is $(1\\,000,200).$ Let's write the ratio $1\\,000:200$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,000}{200}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by $200:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,000÷200}{200÷200}=\\frac{5}{1}\n$$\n\n So the ratio of red paint to yellow paint is $5:1.$"}]}
